OL,3,GNEWSACanal bank breached and homes
OL,4,Aflooded after pipe collapse
OL,5,
OL,6,FA canal bank has been breached,
OL,7,Fflooding two homes, after a pipe
OL,8,Fcarrying water underneath it collapsed.
OL,10,FThe Canal and River Trust (CRT) said it
OL,11,Fwas responding to an incident on the
OL,12,FLlangollen Canal at Hampton Bank in
OL,13,FShropshire following the collapse of
OL,14,Fthe pipe, known as a culvert.
OL,16,FA CRT spokesperson said its team along
OL,17,Fwith infrastructure partner, Kier, were
OL,18,Fon site and had closed the affected
OL,19,Fsection of canal. The trust added it
OL,20,Fwas carrying out emergency works to
OL,21,Fslow the flow of water into a
OL,22,Fneighbouring field.
OL,23,APub: 13-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
